IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc18-forfeiture.l4 -- the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46, sections 490.1 to 490.9 (forfeiture of offence-related property: on conviction, in rem,
-- notice, restoration, non-forfeiture, third-party applications, suspension, restraint orders, management orders). Part agent ccc18; layer 1. Answers are MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- (or MAYBE / total types where the text closes the list): JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE (the text says no in its own words), NOTHING (not covered). A "may" function whose "if" gate
-- fails answers NOTHING (ruling of 2026-11-12 (1)); a "may" function whose gate is "where" answers JUST FALSE (periods ruling (b)) and carries `[may-where]`: NOTES.md, fork register.
-- A judgment the text hands to a court or judge ("if satisfied that ...") is a BOOLEAN input. `s 2 offence-related property` is taken from the keel as a MAYBE BOOLEAN input
-- (PLAN.md section 4). See the header of `ccc18-soira-notice` and NOTES.md.

§ `Sections 490.1 to 490.9 -- Forfeiture of offence-related property`

§ `490.1 Order of forfeiture of property on conviction`

-- src:10703 | Forfeiture of Offence-related Property
-- src:10704 | Order of forfeiture of property on conviction
-- src:10705 | 490.1 (1) Subject to sections 490.3 to 490.41, if a person is convicted, or discharged under section 730, of an indictable offence under this Act or the Corruption of Foreign Public Officials Act and, on application of the Attorney General, the court is satisfied, on a balance of probabilities, that offence-related property is related to the commission of the offence, the court shall
-- src:10706 | (a) if the prosecution of the offence was commenced at the instance of the government of a province and conducted by or on behalf of that government, order that the property be forfeited to Her Majesty in right of that province to be disposed of or otherwise dealt with in accordance with the law by the Attorney General or Solicitor General of that province; and
-- src:10707 | (b) in any other case, order that the property be forfeited to Her Majesty in right of Canada to be disposed of or otherwise dealt with in accordance with the law by the member of the Queen’s Privy Council for Canada that is designated by the Governor in Council for the purpose of this paragraph.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.1(1) (src:10703-10707)
DECLARE `s 490.1(1) the Crown to which the property is forfeited` IS ONE OF
    `s 490.1(1)(a) Her Majesty in right of the province, to be disposed of or otherwise dealt with by the Attorney General or Solicitor General of that province`
    `s 490.1(1)(b) Her Majesty in right of Canada, to be disposed of or otherwise dealt with by the member of the Privy Council for Canada designated by the Governor in Council`

@ref Criminal Code s 490.1(1) (src:10703-10707)
GIVEN `the person is convicted, or discharged under section 730, of an indictable offence under this Act or the Corruption of Foreign Public Officials Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `on application of the Attorney General, the court is satisfied, on a balance of probabilities, that the property is related to the commission of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 2 offence-related property: the property is offence-related property` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.1(1) the court shall order the property forfeited` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the person is convicted, or discharged under section 730, of an indictable offence under this Act or the Corruption of Foreign Public Officials Act`) OR (NOT `on application of the Attorney General, the court is satisfied, on a balance of probabilities, that the property is related to the commission of the offence`)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if a person is convicted, or discharged under section 730, of an indictable offence under this Act or the Corruption of Foreign Public Officials Act and, on application of the Attorney General, the court is satisfied, on a balance of probabilities" [marginal (a)]
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 2 offence-related property: the property is offence-related property`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "that offence-related property is related to the commission of the offence" (the property is not offence-related property, which s 2 defines with "means")
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "offence-related property" is defined in section 2, answered by the keel

@ref Criminal Code s 490.1(1) (src:10703-10707)
GIVEN `the prosecution of the offence was commenced at the instance of the government of a province and conducted by or on behalf of that government` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 490.1(1) the Crown to which the property is forfeited`
`s 490.1(1) the Crown in whose right the property is forfeited` MEANS
    IF `the prosecution of the offence was commenced at the instance of the government of a province and conducted by or on behalf of that government`
    THEN `s 490.1(1)(a) Her Majesty in right of the province, to be disposed of or otherwise dealt with by the Attorney General or Solicitor General of that province`
    ELSE `s 490.1(1)(b) Her Majesty in right of Canada, to be disposed of or otherwise dealt with by the member of the Privy Council for Canada designated by the Governor in Council`   -- "(b) in any other case"

@ref Criminal Code s 490.1(1) (src:10703-10707)
GIVEN `the answer of s 490.1(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the court returns the property under subsection 490.4(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court decides under subsection 490.41(3) not to order the forfeiture of the property` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.1(1) the court shall order the property forfeited, subject to sections 490.3 to 490.41` MEANS
    IF `the court returns the property under subsection 490.4(3)` OR `the court decides under subsection 490.41(3) not to order the forfeiture of the property`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subject to sections 490.3 to 490.41" (the orders of 490.4(3) and 490.41(3) prevail: fork F10)
    ELSE `the answer of s 490.1(1)`

@ref Criminal Code s 490.1(1) (src:10703-10707)
DECLARE `s 490.1(1) action` IS ONE OF `s 490.1(1) order that the property be forfeited to Her Majesty`

@ref Criminal Code s 490.1(1) (src:10703-10707)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 490.1(1) action`
`s 490.1(1) the duty of the court to order the forfeiture` MEANS
    PARTY `the court`
    MUST `s 490.1(1) order that the property be forfeited to Her Majesty`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the court` BECAUSE "the court was satisfied and did not order the property forfeited"

-- src:10709 | Property related to other offences
-- src:10710 | (2) Subject to sections 490.3 to 490.41, if the evidence does not establish to the satisfaction of the court that property in respect of which an order of forfeiture would otherwise be made under subsection (1) is related to the commission of the indictable offence under this Act or the Corruption of Foreign Public Officials Act of which a person is convicted or discharged, but the court is satisfied, beyond a reasonable doubt, that the property is offence-related property, the court may make an order of forfeiture under subsection (1) in relation to that property.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.1(2) (src:10709-10710)
GIVEN `the evidence does not establish to the satisfaction of the court that the property is related to the commission of the indictable offence of which the person is convicted or discharged` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied, beyond a reasonable doubt, that the property is offence-related property` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.1(2) the court may make an order of forfeiture under subsection (1) of property not shown to be related to the offence` MEANS
    IF `the evidence does not establish to the satisfaction of the court that the property is related to the commission of the indictable offence of which the person is convicted or discharged` AND `the court is satisfied, beyond a reasonable doubt, that the property is offence-related property`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the court may make an order of forfeiture under subsection (1) in relation to that property"

-- src:10711 | Property outside Canada
-- src:10712 | (2.1) An order may be issued under this section in respect of property situated outside Canada, with any modifications that the circumstances require.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.1(2.1) (src:10711-10712)
GIVEN `the property is situated outside Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.1(2.1) an order may be issued in respect of property situated outside Canada` MEANS
    IF `the property is situated outside Canada`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An order may be issued under this section in respect of property situated outside Canada"

-- src:10713 | Appeal
-- src:10714 | (3) A person who has been convicted of an indictable offence under this Act or the Corruption of Foreign Public Officials Act, or the Attorney General, may appeal to the court of appeal from an order or a failure to make an order under subsection (1) as if the appeal were an appeal against the sentence imposed on the person in respect of the offence.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.1(3) (src:10713-10714)
DECLARE `s 490.1(3) appellant` IS ONE OF
    `s 490.1(3) a person convicted of an indictable offence under this Act or the Corruption of Foreign Public Officials Act`
    `s 490.1(3) the Attorney General`
    `s 490.1(3) another person`

@ref Criminal Code s 490.1(3) (src:10713-10714)
GIVEN appellant IS A `s 490.1(3) appellant`
      `the appeal is from an order or a failure to make an order under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appeal is brought as if it were an appeal against the sentence imposed on the person in respect of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.1(3) the appeal may be brought` MEANS
    IF appellant EQUALS `s 490.1(3) another person` OR (NOT `the appeal is from an order or a failure to make an order under subsection (1)`) OR (NOT `the appeal is brought as if it were an appeal against the sentence imposed on the person in respect of the offence`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may appeal to the court of appeal from an order or a failure to make an order under subsection (1) as if the appeal were an appeal against the sentence imposed on the person in respect of the offence"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

§ `490.2 Application for in rem forfeiture`

-- src:10715 | Application for in rem forfeiture
-- src:10716 | 490.2 (1) If an information has been laid in respect of an indictable offence under this Act or the Corruption of Foreign Public Officials Act, the Attorney General may make an application to a judge for an order of forfeiture under subsection (2).
@ref Criminal Code s 490.2(1) (src:10715-10716)
GIVEN `an information has been laid in respect of an indictable offence under this Act or the Corruption of Foreign Public Officials Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicant is the Attorney General` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.2(1) the Attorney General may make an application to a judge for an order of forfeiture` MEANS
    IF `an information has been laid in respect of an indictable offence under this Act or the Corruption of Foreign Public Officials Act` AND `the applicant is the Attorney General`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the Attorney General may make an application to a judge for an order of forfeiture under subsection (2)"

-- src:10717 | Order of forfeiture of property
-- src:10718 | (2) Subject to sections 490.3 to 490.41, the judge to whom an application is made under subsection (1) shall order that the property that is subject to the application be forfeited and disposed of in accordance with subsection (4) if the judge is satisfied
-- src:10719 | (a) beyond a reasonable doubt that the property is offence-related property;
-- src:10720 | (b) that proceedings in respect of an indictable offence under this Act or the Corruption of Foreign Public Officials Act in relation to the property were commenced; and
-- src:10721 | (c) that the accused charged with the offence has died or absconded.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.2(2) (src:10717-10721)
GIVEN `(a) the judge is satisfied beyond a reasonable doubt that the property is offence-related property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `(b) the judge is satisfied that proceedings in respect of an indictable offence under this Act or the Corruption of Foreign Public Officials Act in relation to the property were commenced` IS A BOOLEAN
      `(c) the judge is satisfied that the accused charged with the offence has died or absconded` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.2(2) the judge shall order the property forfeited` MEANS
    IF `(a) the judge is satisfied beyond a reasonable doubt that the property is offence-related property`
       AND `(b) the judge is satisfied that proceedings in respect of an indictable offence under this Act or the Corruption of Foreign Public Officials Act in relation to the property were commenced`
       AND `(c) the judge is satisfied that the accused charged with the offence has died or absconded`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall order that the property that is subject to the application be forfeited and disposed of in accordance with subsection (4) if the judge is satisfied" [marginal (a)]

@ref Criminal Code s 490.2(2) (src:10717-10721)
DECLARE `s 490.2(2) action` IS ONE OF `s 490.2(2) order that the property be forfeited and disposed of in accordance with subsection (4)`

@ref Criminal Code s 490.2(2) (src:10717-10721)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 490.2(2) action`
`s 490.2(2) the duty of the judge to order the forfeiture` MEANS
    PARTY `a judge`
    MUST `s 490.2(2) order that the property be forfeited and disposed of in accordance with subsection (4)`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `a judge` BECAUSE "the judge was satisfied of the three matters and did not order the forfeiture"

-- src:10717 | Order of forfeiture of property
-- src:10718 | (2) Subject to sections 490.3 to 490.41, the judge to whom an application is made under subsection (1) shall order that the property that is subject to the application be forfeited and disposed of in accordance with subsection (4) if the judge is satisfied
-- src:10719 | (a) beyond a reasonable doubt that the property is offence-related property;
-- src:10720 | (b) that proceedings in respect of an indictable offence under this Act or the Corruption of Foreign Public Officials Act in relation to the property were commenced; and
-- src:10721 | (c) that the accused charged with the offence has died or absconded.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.2(2) (src:10717-10721)
GIVEN `the answer of s 490.2(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the court returns the property under subsection 490.4(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court decides under subsection 490.41(3) not to order the forfeiture of the property` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.2(2) the judge shall order the property forfeited, subject to sections 490.3 to 490.41` MEANS
    IF `the court returns the property under subsection 490.4(3)` OR `the court decides under subsection 490.41(3) not to order the forfeiture of the property`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subject to sections 490.3 to 490.41" (the orders of 490.4(3) and 490.41(3) prevail: fork F10)
    ELSE `the answer of s 490.2(2)`

-- src:10722 | Accused deemed absconded
-- src:10723 | (3) For the purpose of subsection (2), an accused is deemed to have absconded in connection with the indictable offence if
-- src:10724 | (a) an information has been laid alleging the commission of the offence by the accused,
-- src:10725 | (b) a warrant for the arrest of the accused has been issued in relation to that information, and
-- src:10726 | (c) reasonable attempts to arrest the accused under the warrant have been unsuccessful during a period of six months beginning on the day on which the warrant was issued,
-- src:10727 | and the accused is deemed to have so absconded on the last day of that six month period.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.2(3) (src:10722-10727)
GIVEN `(a) an information has been laid alleging the commission of the offence by the accused` IS A BOOLEAN
      `(b) a warrant for the arrest of the accused has been issued in relation to that information` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the warrant was issued` IS A DATE
      `(c) reasonable attempts to arrest the accused under the warrant have been unsuccessful during a period of six months beginning on the day on which the warrant was issued` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 490.2(3) the day on which the accused is deemed to have absconded` MEANS
    IF `(a) an information has been laid alleging the commission of the offence by the accused` AND `(b) a warrant for the arrest of the accused has been issued in relation to that information` AND `(c) reasonable attempts to arrest the accused under the warrant have been unsuccessful during a period of six months beginning on the day on which the warrant was issued`
    THEN JUST (Date (DATE_DAY `the day on which the warrant was issued` MINUS 1) (DATE_MONTH `the day on which the warrant was issued` PLUS 6) (DATE_YEAR `the day on which the warrant was issued`))   -- "the last day of that six month period": the period begins on the day of issue, so it ends the day before the same date six months later
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an accused is deemed to have absconded in connection with the indictable offence if"; a deeming, so outside it the subsection says nothing (a person may still have absconded in fact)

-- src:10728 | Who may dispose of forfeited property
-- src:10729 | (4) For the purpose of subsection (2), the judge shall
-- src:10730 | (a) if the prosecution of the offence was commenced at the instance of the government of a province and conducted by or on behalf of that government, order that the property be forfeited to Her Majesty in right of that province to be disposed of or otherwise dealt with in accordance with the law by the Attorney General or Solicitor General of that province; and
-- src:10731 | (b) in any other case, order that the property be forfeited to Her Majesty in right of Canada to be disposed of or otherwise dealt with in accordance with the law by the member of the Queen’s Privy Council for Canada that is designated by the Governor in Council for the purpose of this paragraph.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.2(4) (src:10728-10731)
GIVEN `the prosecution of the offence was commenced at the instance of the government of a province and conducted by or on behalf of that government` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 490.1(1) the Crown to which the property is forfeited`
`s 490.2(4) the Crown in whose right the judge shall order the property forfeited` MEANS
    IF `the prosecution of the offence was commenced at the instance of the government of a province and conducted by or on behalf of that government`
    THEN `s 490.1(1)(a) Her Majesty in right of the province, to be disposed of or otherwise dealt with by the Attorney General or Solicitor General of that province`
    ELSE `s 490.1(1)(b) Her Majesty in right of Canada, to be disposed of or otherwise dealt with by the member of the Privy Council for Canada designated by the Governor in Council`   -- "(b) in any other case"

-- src:10732 | Property outside Canada
-- src:10733 | (4.1) An order may be issued under this section in respect of property situated outside Canada, with any modifications that the circumstances require.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.2(4.1) (src:10732-10733)
GIVEN `the property is situated outside Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.2(4.1) an order may be issued in respect of property situated outside Canada` MEANS
    IF `the property is situated outside Canada`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An order may be issued under this section in respect of property situated outside Canada"

-- src:10734 | Definition of judge
-- src:10735 | (5) In this section and sections 490.5 and 490.8, judge means a judge as defined in section 552 or a judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.2(5) (src:10734-10735)
GIVEN `the person is a judge as defined in section 552, by s 552 judge` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person is a judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.2(5) judge` MEANS
    IF `the person is a judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction` THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE CONSIDER `the person is a judge as defined in section 552, by s 552 judge`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "judge means a judge as defined in section 552 or a judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction"
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "judge" is defined in section 552, answered by another part

§ `490.3 Voidable transfers`

-- src:10736 | Voidable transfers
-- src:10737 | 490.3 A court may, before ordering that offence-related property be forfeited under subsection 490.1(1) or 490.2(2), set aside any conveyance or transfer of the property that occurred after the seizure of the property, or the making of a restraint order in respect of the property, unless the conveyance or transfer was for valuable consideration to a person acting in good faith.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.3 (src:10736-10737)
GIVEN `the conveyance or transfer of the property occurred after the seizure of the property, or the making of a restraint order in respect of the property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the conveyance or transfer was for valuable consideration to a person acting in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.3 the court may set aside the conveyance or transfer` MEANS
    IF `the conveyance or transfer was for valuable consideration to a person acting in good faith`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the conveyance or transfer was for valuable consideration to a person acting in good faith"
    ELSE IF `the conveyance or transfer of the property occurred after the seizure of the property, or the making of a restraint order in respect of the property`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "set aside any conveyance or transfer of the property that occurred after the seizure of the property, or the making of a restraint order"

§ `490.4 Notice; order of restoration of property`

-- src:10738 | Notice
-- src:10739 | 490.4 (1) Before making an order under subsection 490.1(1) or 490.2(2) in relation to any property, a court shall require notice in accordance with subsection (2) to be given to, and may hear, any person who, in the opinion of the court, appears to have a valid interest in the property.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.4(1) (src:10738-10739)
DECLARE `s 490.4(1) action` IS ONE OF `s 490.4(1) require notice in accordance with subsection (2) to be given to the person`

@ref Criminal Code s 490.4(1) (src:10738-10739)
GIVEN `before making an order under subsection 490.1(1) or 490.2(2) in relation to the property, the court is of the opinion that the person appears to have a valid interest in the property` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.4(1) the court shall require notice to be given to the person` MEANS
    IF `before making an order under subsection 490.1(1) or 490.2(2) in relation to the property, the court is of the opinion that the person appears to have a valid interest in the property` THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is laid only where "any person who, in the opinion of the court, appears to have a valid interest in the property"

@ref Criminal Code s 490.4(1) (src:10738-10739)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `s 490.4(1) action`
`s 490.4(1) the duty of the court` MEANS
    PARTY `the court`
    MUST `s 490.4(1) require notice in accordance with subsection (2) to be given to the person`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the court` BECAUSE "the court did not require notice to be given to the person with a valid interest"

-- src:10738 | Notice
-- src:10739 | 490.4 (1) Before making an order under subsection 490.1(1) or 490.2(2) in relation to any property, a court shall require notice in accordance with subsection (2) to be given to, and may hear, any person who, in the opinion of the court, appears to have a valid interest in the property.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.4(1) (src:10738-10739)
GIVEN `before making an order under subsection 490.1(1) or 490.2(2) in relation to the property, the court is of the opinion that the person appears to have a valid interest in the property` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.4(1) (hearing) the court may hear the person` MEANS
    IF `before making an order under subsection 490.1(1) or 490.2(2) in relation to the property, the court is of the opinion that the person appears to have a valid interest in the property`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "and may hear, any person who, in the opinion of the court, appears to have a valid interest in the property"

-- src:10740 | Manner of giving notice
-- src:10741 | (2) A notice shall
-- src:10742 | (a) be given in the manner that the court directs or that may be specified in the rules of the court;
-- src:10743 | (b) specify the period that the court considers reasonable or that may be set out in the rules of the court during which a person may make an application to the court asserting their interest in the property; and
-- src:10744 | (c) set out the offence charged and a description of the property.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.4(2) (src:10740-10744)
GIVEN `(a) the notice is given in the manner that the court directs or that may be specified in the rules of the court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `(b) the notice specifies the period that the court considers reasonable or that may be set out in the rules of the court during which a person may make an application to the court asserting their interest in the property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `(c) the notice sets out the offence charged and a description of the property` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.4(2) the notice is as the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `(a) the notice is given in the manner that the court directs or that may be specified in the rules of the court` AND `(b) the notice specifies the period that the court considers reasonable or that may be set out in the rules of the court during which a person may make an application to the court asserting their interest in the property` AND `(c) the notice sets out the offence charged and a description of the property`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A notice shall (a) be given in the manner that the court directs"

-- src:10745 | Order of restoration of property
-- src:10746 | (3) A court may order that all or part of the property that would otherwise be forfeited under subsection 490.1(1) or 490.2(2) be returned to a person — other than a person who was charged with an indictable offence under this Act or the Corruption of Foreign Public Officials Act or a person who acquired title to or a right of possession of the property from such a person under circumstances that give rise to a reasonable inference that the title or right was transferred for the purpose of avoiding the forfeiture of the property — if the court is satisfied that the person is the lawful owner or is lawfully entitled to possession of all or part of that property, and that the person appears innocent of any complicity in, or collusion in relation to, the offence.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.4(3) (src:10745-10746)
GIVEN `the person was charged with an indictable offence under this Act or the Corruption of Foreign Public Officials Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person acquired title to or a right of possession of the property from such a person under circumstances that give rise to a reasonable inference that the title or right was transferred for the purpose of avoiding the forfeiture of the property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that the person is the lawful owner or is lawfully entitled to possession of all or part of that property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that the person appears innocent of any complicity in, or collusion in relation to, the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.4(3) the court may order that the property be returned to the person` MEANS
    IF `the person was charged with an indictable offence under this Act or the Corruption of Foreign Public Officials Act` OR `the person acquired title to or a right of possession of the property from such a person under circumstances that give rise to a reasonable inference that the title or right was transferred for the purpose of avoiding the forfeiture of the property`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "be returned to a person — other than a person who was charged with an indictable offence under this Act or the Corruption of Foreign Public Officials Act" (fork F11: "other than" read as an exclusion)
    ELSE IF `the court is satisfied that the person is the lawful owner or is lawfully entitled to possession of all or part of that property` AND `the court is satisfied that the person appears innocent of any complicity in, or collusion in relation to, the offence`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the court is satisfied that the person is the lawful owner or is lawfully entitled to possession of all or part of that property, and that the person appears innocent" (fork F5: the other reading is JUST FALSE)

§ `490.41 Notice: dwelling-house; non-forfeiture of property`

-- src:10747 | Notice
-- src:10748 | 490.41 (1) If all or part of offence-related property that would otherwise be forfeited under subsection 490.1(1) or 490.2(2) is a dwelling-house, before making an order of forfeiture, a court shall require that notice in accordance with subsection (2) be given to, and may hear, any person who resides in the dwelling-house and is a member of the immediate family of the person charged with or convicted of the indictable offence under this Act or the Corruption of Foreign Public Officials Act in relation to which the property would be forfeited.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.41(1) (src:10747-10748)
GIVEN `s 2 dwelling-house: all or part of the offence-related property is a dwelling-house` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person resides in the dwelling-house` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a member of the immediate family of the person charged with or convicted of the indictable offence in relation to which the property would be forfeited` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.41(1) the court shall require notice to be given to the person, and may hear them` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the person resides in the dwelling-house` AND `the person is a member of the immediate family of the person charged with or convicted of the indictable offence in relation to which the property would be forfeited`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any person who resides in the dwelling-house and is a member of the immediate family of the person charged with or convicted"
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 2 dwelling-house: all or part of the offence-related property is a dwelling-house`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is for the case where "If all or part of offence-related property that would otherwise be forfeited under subsection 490.1(1) or 490.2(2) is a dwelling-house"
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "dwelling-house" is defined in section 2, answered by the keel

@ref Criminal Code s 490.41(1) (src:10747-10748)
DECLARE `s 490.41(1) action` IS ONE OF `s 490.41(1) require notice in accordance with subsection (2) to be given to the member of the immediate family who resides in the dwelling-house`

@ref Criminal Code s 490.41(1) (src:10747-10748)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 490.41(1) action`
`s 490.41(1) the duty of the court to require notice to the member of the immediate family` MEANS
    PARTY `the court`
    MUST `s 490.41(1) require notice in accordance with subsection (2) to be given to the member of the immediate family who resides in the dwelling-house`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the court` BECAUSE "the court made an order of forfeiture without requiring notice to the member of the immediate family"

-- src:10749 | Manner of giving notice
-- src:10750 | (2) A notice shall
-- src:10751 | (a) be given in the manner that the court directs or that may be specified in the rules of the court;
-- src:10752 | (b) specify the period that the court considers reasonable or that may be set out in the rules of the court during which a member of the immediate family who resides in the dwelling-house may make themselves known to the court; and
-- src:10753 | (c) set out the offence charged and a description of the property.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.41(2) (src:10749-10753)
GIVEN `(a) the notice is given in the manner that the court directs or that may be specified in the rules of the court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `(b) the notice specifies the period that the court considers reasonable or that may be set out in the rules of the court during which a member of the immediate family who resides in the dwelling-house may make themselves known to the court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `(c) the notice sets out the offence charged and a description of the property` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.41(2) the notice is as the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `(a) the notice is given in the manner that the court directs or that may be specified in the rules of the court` AND `(b) the notice specifies the period that the court considers reasonable or that may be set out in the rules of the court during which a member of the immediate family who resides in the dwelling-house may make themselves known to the court` AND `(c) the notice sets out the offence charged and a description of the property`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A notice shall (a) be given in the manner that the court directs"

-- src:10754 | Non-forfeiture of property
-- src:10755 | (3) Subject to an order made under subsection 490.4(3), if a court is satisfied that the impact of an order of forfeiture made under subsection 490.1(1) or 490.2(2) would be disproportionate to the nature and gravity of the offence, the circumstances surrounding the commission of the offence and the criminal record, if any, of the person charged with or convicted of the offence, as the case may be, it may decide not to order the forfeiture of the property or part of the property and may revoke any restraint order made in respect of that property or part.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.41(3) (src:10754-10755)
GIVEN `the court is satisfied that the impact of an order of forfeiture made under subsection 490.1(1) or 490.2(2) would be disproportionate to the nature and gravity of the offence, the circumstances surrounding the commission of the offence and the criminal record, if any, of the person charged with or convicted of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.41(3) (decision) the court may decide not to order the forfeiture of the property or part of the property` MEANS
    IF `the court is satisfied that the impact of an order of forfeiture made under subsection 490.1(1) or 490.2(2) would be disproportionate to the nature and gravity of the offence, the circumstances surrounding the commission of the offence and the criminal record, if any, of the person charged with or convicted of the offence`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if a court is satisfied that the impact of an order of forfeiture made under subsection 490.1(1) or 490.2(2) would be disproportionate"

-- src:10754 | Non-forfeiture of property
-- src:10755 | (3) Subject to an order made under subsection 490.4(3), if a court is satisfied that the impact of an order of forfeiture made under subsection 490.1(1) or 490.2(2) would be disproportionate to the nature and gravity of the offence, the circumstances surrounding the commission of the offence and the criminal record, if any, of the person charged with or convicted of the offence, as the case may be, it may decide not to order the forfeiture of the property or part of the property and may revoke any restraint order made in respect of that property or part.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.41(3) (src:10754-10755)
GIVEN `the court is satisfied that the impact of an order of forfeiture made under subsection 490.1(1) or 490.2(2) would be disproportionate to the nature and gravity of the offence, the circumstances surrounding the commission of the offence and the criminal record, if any, of the person charged with or convicted of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.41(3) (restraint order) the court may revoke a restraint order made in respect of the property or part of it` MEANS
    IF `the court is satisfied that the impact of an order of forfeiture made under subsection 490.1(1) or 490.2(2) would be disproportionate to the nature and gravity of the offence, the circumstances surrounding the commission of the offence and the criminal record, if any, of the person charged with or convicted of the offence`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "and may revoke any restraint order made in respect of that property or part"

-- src:10756 | Factors in relation to dwelling-house
-- src:10757 | (4) Where all or part of the property that would otherwise be forfeited under subsection 490.1(1) or 490.2(2) is a dwelling-house, when making a decision under subsection (3), the court shall also consider
-- src:10758 | (a) the impact of an order of forfeiture on any member of the immediate family of the person charged with or convicted of the offence, if the dwelling-house was the member’s principal residence at the time the charge was laid and continues to be the member’s principal residence; and
-- src:10759 | (b) whether the member referred to in paragraph (a) appears innocent of any complicity in the offence or of any collusion in relation to the offence.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.41(4) (src:10756-10759)
DECLARE `s 490.41(4) what the court shall also consider` IS ONE OF
    `s 490.41(4)(a) the impact of an order of forfeiture on any member of the immediate family of the person charged with or convicted of the offence, if the dwelling-house was the member’s principal residence at the time the charge was laid and continues to be the member’s principal residence`
    `s 490.41(4)(b) whether the member referred to in paragraph (a) appears innocent of any complicity in the offence or of any collusion in relation to the offence`
    `s 490.41(4) a matter outside paragraphs (a) and (b)`

@ref Criminal Code s 490.41(4) (src:10756-10759)
GIVEN `s 2 dwelling-house: all or part of the property that would otherwise be forfeited is a dwelling-house` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the court is making a decision under subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      matter IS A `s 490.41(4) what the court shall also consider`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.41(4) the court shall also consider the matter` MEANS
    IF NOT `the court is making a decision under subsection (3)`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "when making a decision under subsection (3), the court shall also consider" [marginal (a)]
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 2 dwelling-house: all or part of the property that would otherwise be forfeited is a dwelling-house`
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where all or part of the property that would otherwise be forfeited under subsection 490.1(1) or 490.2(2) is a dwelling-house" [marginal (a)]
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "dwelling-house" is defined in section 2, answered by the keel
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
             CONSIDER matter
             WHEN `s 490.41(4)(a) the impact of an order of forfeiture on any member of the immediate family of the person charged with or convicted of the offence, if the dwelling-house was the member’s principal residence at the time the charge was laid and continues to be the member’s principal residence` THEN JUST TRUE
             WHEN `s 490.41(4)(b) whether the member referred to in paragraph (a) appears innocent of any complicity in the offence or of any collusion in relation to the offence` THEN JUST TRUE
             WHEN `s 490.41(4) a matter outside paragraphs (a) and (b)` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the court "shall also consider" the two matters listed

§ `490.5 Application by a person claiming an interest`

-- src:10760 | Application
-- src:10761 | 490.5 (1) Where any offence-related property is forfeited to Her Majesty pursuant to an order made under subsection 490.1(1) or 490.2(2), any person who claims an interest in the property, other than
-- src:10762 | (a) in the case of property forfeited pursuant to an order made under subsection 490.1(1), a person who was convicted of the indictable offence in relation to which the property was forfeited,
-- src:10763 | (b) in the case of property forfeited pursuant to an order made under subsection 490.2(2), a person who was charged with the indictable offence in relation to which the property was forfeited, or
-- src:10764 | (c) a person who acquired title to or a right of possession of the property from a person referred to in paragraph (a) or (b) under circumstances that give rise to a reasonable inference that the title or right was transferred from that person for the purpose of avoiding the forfeiture of the property,
-- src:10765 | may, within thirty days after the forfeiture, apply by notice in writing to a judge for an order under subsection (4).
@ref Criminal Code s 490.5(1) (src:10760-10765)
DECLARE `s 490.5(1) order under which the property was forfeited` IS ONE OF
    `s 490.5(1) an order under subsection 490.1(1)`
    `s 490.5(1) an order under subsection 490.2(2)`

@ref Criminal Code s 490.5(1) (src:10760-10765)
GIVEN order IS A `s 490.5(1) order under which the property was forfeited`
      `they claim an interest in the property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `(a) they were convicted of the indictable offence in relation to which the property was forfeited` IS A BOOLEAN
      `(b) they were charged with the indictable offence in relation to which the property was forfeited` IS A BOOLEAN
      `(c) they acquired title to or a right of possession of the property from a person referred to in paragraph (a) or (b) under circumstances that give rise to a reasonable inference that the title or right was transferred from that person for the purpose of avoiding the forfeiture of the property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the forfeiture` IS A DATE
      `the day on which they apply` IS A DATE
      `they apply by notice in writing to a judge` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.5(1) the person may apply for an order under subsection (4)` MEANS
    IF (order EQUALS `s 490.5(1) an order under subsection 490.1(1)` AND `(a) they were convicted of the indictable offence in relation to which the property was forfeited`)
       OR (order EQUALS `s 490.5(1) an order under subsection 490.2(2)` AND `(b) they were charged with the indictable offence in relation to which the property was forfeited`)
       OR `(c) they acquired title to or a right of possession of the property from a person referred to in paragraph (a) or (b) under circumstances that give rise to a reasonable inference that the title or right was transferred from that person for the purpose of avoiding the forfeiture of the property`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "any person who claims an interest in the property, other than (a) in the case of property forfeited pursuant to an order made under subsection 490.1(1), a person who was convicted of the indictable offence" (fork F11: "other than" read as an exclusion)
    ELSE IF `the day on which they apply` LESS THAN `the day of the forfeiture` OR `the day on which they apply` GREATER THAN `thirty days after` `the day of the forfeiture`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may, within thirty days after the forfeiture, apply by notice in writing to a judge"
         ELSE IF `they claim an interest in the property` AND `they apply by notice in writing to a judge`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may, within thirty days after the forfeiture, apply by notice in writing to a judge for an order under subsection (4)"
    WHERE
        `thirty days after` d MEANS Date (DATE_DAY d PLUS 30) (DATE_MONTH d) (DATE_YEAR d)

-- src:10766 | Fixing day for hearing
-- src:10767 | (2) The judge to whom an application is made under subsection (1) shall fix a day not less than thirty days after the date of the filing of the application for the hearing of the application.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.5(2) (src:10766-10767)
GIVEN `the day of the filing of the application` IS A DATE
      `the day fixed for the hearing of the application` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.5(2) the day fixed is not less than thirty days after the date of the filing` MEANS
    IF `the day fixed for the hearing of the application` AT LEAST Date (DATE_DAY `the day of the filing of the application` PLUS 30) (DATE_MONTH `the day of the filing of the application`) (DATE_YEAR `the day of the filing of the application`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall fix a day not less than thirty days after the date of the filing of the application"

@ref Criminal Code s 490.5(2) (src:10766-10767)
DECLARE `s 490.5(2) action` IS ONE OF `s 490.5(2) fix a day not less than thirty days after the date of the filing of the application for the hearing of the application`

@ref Criminal Code s 490.5(2) (src:10766-10767)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 490.5(2) action`
`s 490.5(2) the duty of the judge to fix the day` MEANS
    PARTY `a judge`
    MUST `s 490.5(2) fix a day not less than thirty days after the date of the filing of the application for the hearing of the application`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `a judge` BECAUSE "the judge did not fix a day for the hearing"

-- src:10768 | Notice
-- src:10769 | (3) An applicant shall serve a notice of the application made under subsection (1) and of the hearing of it on the Attorney General at least fifteen days before the day fixed for the hearing.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.5(3) (src:10768-10769)
GIVEN `the day on which the applicant serves the notice of the application and of the hearing on the Attorney General` IS A DATE
      `the day fixed for the hearing` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.5(3) the notice was served at least fifteen days before the day fixed for the hearing` MEANS
    IF Date (DATE_DAY `the day on which the applicant serves the notice of the application and of the hearing on the Attorney General` PLUS 15) (DATE_MONTH `the day on which the applicant serves the notice of the application and of the hearing on the Attorney General`) (DATE_YEAR `the day on which the applicant serves the notice of the application and of the hearing on the Attorney General`) AT MOST `the day fixed for the hearing`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall serve a notice of the application made under subsection (1) and of the hearing of it on the Attorney General at least fifteen days before the day fixed for the hearing"

@ref Criminal Code s 490.5(3) (src:10768-10769)
DECLARE `s 490.5(3) party` IS ONE OF `s 490.5(3) the applicant`   -- not in the core's Party: NEEDS-CORE.md
DECLARE `s 490.5(3) action` IS ONE OF `s 490.5(3) serve a notice of the application and of the hearing on the Attorney General`

@ref Criminal Code s 490.5(3) (src:10768-10769)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 490.5(3) party` `s 490.5(3) action`
`s 490.5(3) the duty of the applicant to serve the notice` MEANS
    PARTY `s 490.5(3) the applicant`
    MUST `s 490.5(3) serve a notice of the application and of the hearing on the Attorney General`
    WITHIN 15   -- the last day for service is fifteen days before the day fixed for the hearing: the trace's day 0 is the day the hearing is fixed minus fifteen days less the days allowed (fork F12)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 490.5(3) the applicant` BECAUSE "the applicant did not serve the notice on the Attorney General at least fifteen days before the day fixed for the hearing"

-- src:10770 | Order declaring interest not affected by forfeiture
-- src:10771 | (4) Where, on the hearing of an application made under subsection (1), the judge is satisfied that the applicant
-- src:10772 | (a) is not a person referred to in paragraph (1)(a), (b) or (c) and appears innocent of any complicity in any indictable offence that resulted in the forfeiture of the property or of any collusion in relation to such an offence, and
-- src:10773 | (b) exercised all reasonable care to be satisfied that the property was not likely to have been used in connection with the commission of an unlawful act by the person who was permitted by the applicant to obtain possession of the property or from whom the applicant obtained possession or, where the applicant is a mortgagee or lienholder, by the mortgagor or lien-giver,
-- src:10774 | the judge may make an order declaring that the interest of the applicant is not affected by the forfeiture and declaring the nature and the extent or value of the interest.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.5(4) (src:10770-10774)
GIVEN `(a) the judge is satisfied that the applicant is not a person referred to in paragraph (1)(a), (b) or (c) and appears innocent of any complicity in any indictable offence that resulted in the forfeiture of the property or of any collusion in relation to such an offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `(b) the judge is satisfied that the applicant exercised all reasonable care to be satisfied that the property was not likely to have been used in connection with the commission of an unlawful act by the person who was permitted by the applicant to obtain possession of the property or from whom the applicant obtained possession or, where the applicant is a mortgagee or lienholder, by the mortgagor or lien-giver` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.5(4) the judge may make an order declaring that the interest of the applicant is not affected by the forfeiture` MEANS
    IF `(a) the judge is satisfied that the applicant is not a person referred to in paragraph (1)(a), (b) or (c) and appears innocent of any complicity in any indictable offence that resulted in the forfeiture of the property or of any collusion in relation to such an offence` AND `(b) the judge is satisfied that the applicant exercised all reasonable care to be satisfied that the property was not likely to have been used in connection with the commission of an unlawful act by the person who was permitted by the applicant to obtain possession of the property or from whom the applicant obtained possession or, where the applicant is a mortgagee or lienholder, by the mortgagor or lien-giver`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where, on the hearing of an application made under subsection (1), the judge is satisfied that the applicant" [may-where]

-- src:10775 | Appeal from order made under subsection (4)
-- src:10776 | (5) An applicant or the Attorney General may appeal to the court of appeal from an order made under subsection (4), and the provisions of Part XXI with respect to procedure on appeals apply, with any modifications that the circumstances require, in respect of appeals under this subsection.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.5(5) (src:10775-10776)
DECLARE `s 490.5(5) appellant` IS ONE OF
    `s 490.5(5) an applicant`
    `s 490.5(5) the Attorney General`
    `s 490.5(5) another person`

@ref Criminal Code s 490.5(5) (src:10775-10776)
GIVEN appellant IS A `s 490.5(5) appellant`
      `the appeal is from an order made under subsection (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appeal is to the court of appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.5(5) the appeal may be brought` MEANS
    IF appellant EQUALS `s 490.5(5) another person` OR (NOT `the appeal is from an order made under subsection (4)`) OR (NOT `the appeal is to the court of appeal`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An applicant or the Attorney General may appeal to the court of appeal from an order made under subsection (4)"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:10777 | Return of property
-- src:10778 | (6) The Attorney General shall, on application made to the Attorney General by any person in respect of whom a judge has made an order under subsection (4), and where the periods with respect to the taking of appeals from that order have expired and any appeal from that order taken under subsection (5) has been determined, direct that
-- src:10779 | (a) the property, or the part of it to which the interest of the applicant relates, be returned to the applicant; or
-- src:10780 | (b) an amount equal to the value of the interest of the applicant, as declared in the order, be paid to the applicant.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.5(6) (src:10777-10780)
DECLARE `s 490.5(6) action` IS ONE OF `s 490.5(6) direct that the property, or the part of it to which the interest of the applicant relates, be returned to the applicant, or that an amount equal to the value of the interest of the applicant, as declared in the order, be paid to the applicant`

@ref Criminal Code s 490.5(6) (src:10777-10780)
GIVEN `an application is made to the Attorney General by a person in respect of whom a judge has made an order under subsection (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the periods with respect to the taking of appeals from that order have expired` IS A BOOLEAN
      `any appeal from that order taken under subsection (5) has been determined` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.5(6) the Attorney General shall direct that the property be returned or the amount paid` MEANS
    IF `an application is made to the Attorney General by a person in respect of whom a judge has made an order under subsection (4)` AND `the periods with respect to the taking of appeals from that order have expired` AND `any appeal from that order taken under subsection (5) has been determined`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall, on application made to the Attorney General by any person in respect of whom a judge has made an order under subsection (4), and where the periods with respect to the taking of appeals from that order have expired" [marginal (a)]

@ref Criminal Code s 490.5(6) (src:10777-10780)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 490.5(6) action`
`s 490.5(6) the duty of the Attorney General to direct the return or the payment` MEANS
    PARTY `the Attorney General`
    MUST `s 490.5(6) direct that the property, or the part of it to which the interest of the applicant relates, be returned to the applicant, or that an amount equal to the value of the interest of the applicant, as declared in the order, be paid to the applicant`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the Attorney General` BECAUSE "the Attorney General did not direct the return of the property or the payment"

§ `490.6 Appeals from orders under subsection 490.2(2); 490.7 Suspension of order pending appeal`

-- src:10781 | Appeals from orders under subsection 490.2(2)
-- src:10782 | 490.6 Any person who, in their opinion, is aggrieved by an order made under subsection 490.2(2) may appeal from the order as if the order were an appeal against conviction or against a judgment or verdict of acquittal, as the case may be, under Part XXI, and that Part applies, with any modifications that the circumstances require, in respect of such an appeal.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.6 (src:10781-10782)
GIVEN `in their opinion, the person is aggrieved by an order made under subsection 490.2(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.6 the person may appeal from the order` MEANS
    IF `in their opinion, the person is aggrieved by an order made under subsection 490.2(2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any person who, in their opinion, is aggrieved by an order made under subsection 490.2(2) may appeal from the order"

-- src:10783 | Suspension of order pending appeal
-- src:10784 | 490.7 Notwithstanding anything in this Act, the operation of an order made in respect of property under subsection 490.1(1), 490.2(2) or 490.5(4) is suspended pending
-- src:10785 | (a) any application made in respect of the property under any of those provisions or any other provision of this or any other Act of Parliament that provides for restoration or forfeiture of the property, or
-- src:10786 | (b) any appeal taken from an order of forfeiture or restoration in respect of the property,
-- src:10787 | and the property shall not be disposed of or otherwise dealt with until thirty days have expired after an order is made under any of those provisions.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.7 (src:10783-10787)
GIVEN `(a) an application is pending in respect of the property under any of those provisions or any other provision of this or any other Act of Parliament that provides for restoration or forfeiture of the property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `(b) an appeal is pending from an order of forfeiture or restoration in respect of the property` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.7 the operation of the order is suspended` MEANS
    IF `(a) an application is pending in respect of the property under any of those provisions or any other provision of this or any other Act of Parliament that provides for restoration or forfeiture of the property` OR `(b) an appeal is pending from an order of forfeiture or restoration in respect of the property`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the operation of an order made in respect of property under subsection 490.1(1), 490.2(2) or 490.5(4) is suspended pending" [marginal (a)]

@ref Criminal Code s 490.7 (src:10783-10787)
GIVEN `the day on which the order is made` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the property is disposed of or otherwise dealt with` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.7 the property shall not be disposed of or otherwise dealt with` MEANS
    IF `the day on which the property is disposed of or otherwise dealt with` AT MOST Date (DATE_DAY `the day on which the order is made` PLUS 30) (DATE_MONTH `the day on which the order is made`) (DATE_YEAR `the day on which the order is made`)
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- the bar applies
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the property shall not be disposed of or otherwise dealt with until thirty days have expired after an order is made" (thirty days having expired: fork F12)

§ `490.8 Application for restraint order`

-- src:10788 | Application for restraint order
-- src:10789 | 490.8 (1) The Attorney General may make an application in accordance with this section for a restraint order under this section in respect of any offence-related property.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.8(1) (src:10788-10789)
GIVEN `s 2 offence-related property: the property is offence-related property` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.8(1) the Attorney General may apply for a restraint order` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 2 offence-related property: the property is offence-related property`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for a restraint order under this section in respect of any offence-related property"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "offence-related property" is defined in section 2, answered by the keel

-- src:10790 | Procedure
-- src:10791 | (2) An application made under subsection (1) for a restraint order in respect of any offence-related property may be made ex parte and shall be made in writing to a judge and be accompanied by an affidavit sworn on the information and belief of the Attorney General or any other person deposing to the following matters:
-- src:10792 | (a) the indictable offence to which the offence-related property relates;
-- src:10793 | (b) the person who is believed to be in possession of the offence-related property; and
-- src:10794 | (c) a description of the offence-related property.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.8(2) (src:10790-10794)
GIVEN `the application is made in writing to a judge` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is accompanied by an affidavit sworn on the information and belief of the Attorney General or any other person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the affidavit deposes to (a) the indictable offence to which the offence-related property relates, (b) the person who is believed to be in possession of the offence-related property, and (c) a description of the offence-related property` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.8(2) the application is in the form the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `the application is made in writing to a judge` AND `the application is accompanied by an affidavit sworn on the information and belief of the Attorney General or any other person` AND `the affidavit deposes to (a) the indictable offence to which the offence-related property relates, (b) the person who is believed to be in possession of the offence-related property, and (c) a description of the offence-related property`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be made in writing to a judge and be accompanied by an affidavit sworn on the information and belief of the Attorney General or any other person"

-- src:10795 | Restraint order
-- src:10796 | (3) Where an application for a restraint order is made to a judge under subsection (1), the judge may, if satisfied that there are reasonable grounds to believe that the property is offence-related property, make a restraint order prohibiting any person from disposing of, or otherwise dealing with any interest in, the offence-related property specified in the order otherwise than in the manner that may be specified in the order.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.8(3) (src:10795-10796)
GIVEN `the judge is satisfied that there are reasonable grounds to believe that the property is offence-related property` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.8(3) the judge may make a restraint order` MEANS
    IF `the judge is satisfied that there are reasonable grounds to believe that the property is offence-related property`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the judge may, if satisfied that there are reasonable grounds to believe that the property is offence-related property, make a restraint order"

-- src:10797 | Property outside Canada
-- src:10798 | (3.1) A restraint order may be issued under this section in respect of property situated outside Canada, with any modifications that the circumstances require.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.8(3.1) (src:10797-10798)
GIVEN `the property is situated outside Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.8(3.1) a restraint order may be issued in respect of property situated outside Canada` MEANS
    IF `the property is situated outside Canada`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A restraint order may be issued under this section in respect of property situated outside Canada"

-- src:10799 | Conditions
-- src:10800 | (4) A restraint order made by a judge under this section may be subject to any reasonable conditions that the judge thinks fit.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.8(4) (src:10799-10800)
GIVEN `the condition is one that the judge thinks fit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the condition is reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.8(4) the restraint order may be subject to the condition` MEANS
    IF `the condition is one that the judge thinks fit` AND `the condition is reasonable`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may be subject to any reasonable conditions that the judge thinks fit"

-- src:10801 | Order in writing
-- src:10802 | (5) A restraint order made under this section shall be made in writing.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.8(5) (src:10801-10802)
GIVEN `the restraint order is made in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.8(5) the restraint order is made as the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `the restraint order is made in writing`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A restraint order made under this section shall be made in writing"

-- src:10803 | Service of order
-- src:10804 | (6) A copy of a restraint order made under this section shall be served on the person to whom the order is addressed in any manner that the judge making the order directs or in accordance with the rules of the court.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.8(6) (src:10803-10804)
GIVEN `a copy of the restraint order is served on the person to whom the order is addressed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is served in a manner that the judge making the order directs or in accordance with the rules of the court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.8(6) the copy of the restraint order is served as the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `a copy of the restraint order is served on the person to whom the order is addressed` AND `it is served in a manner that the judge making the order directs or in accordance with the rules of the court`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be served on the person to whom the order is addressed in any manner that the judge making the order directs or in accordance with the rules of the court"

-- src:10805 | Registration of order
-- src:10806 | (7) A copy of a restraint order made under this section shall be registered against any property in accordance with the laws of the province in which the property is situated.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.8(7) (src:10805-10806)
GIVEN `a copy of the restraint order is registered against the property in accordance with the laws of the province in which the property is situated` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.8(7) the copy of the restraint order is registered as the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `a copy of the restraint order is registered against the property in accordance with the laws of the province in which the property is situated`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be registered against any property in accordance with the laws of the province in which the property is situated"

-- src:10807 | Order continues in force
-- src:10808 | (8) A restraint order made under this section remains in effect until
-- src:10809 | (a) an order is made under subsection 490(9) or (11), 490.4(3) or 490.41(3) in relation to the property; or
-- src:10810 | (b) an order of forfeiture of the property is made under section 490 or subsection 490.1(1) or 490.2(2).
@ref Criminal Code s 490.8(8) (src:10807-10810)
GIVEN `(a) an order is made under subsection 490(9) or (11), 490.4(3) or 490.41(3) in relation to the property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `(b) an order of forfeiture of the property is made under section 490 or subsection 490.1(1) or 490.2(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.8(8) the restraint order remains in effect` MEANS
    IF `(a) an order is made under subsection 490(9) or (11), 490.4(3) or 490.41(3) in relation to the property` OR `(b) an order of forfeiture of the property is made under section 490 or subsection 490.1(1) or 490.2(2)`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A restraint order made under this section remains in effect until"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:10811 | Offence
-- src:10812 | (9) Any person on whom a restraint order made under this section is served in accordance with this section and who, while the order is in force, acts in contravention of or fails to comply with the order is guilty of
-- src:10813 | (a) an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than five years; or
-- src:10814 | (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.8(9) (src:10811-10814)
GIVEN `the person is served with a restraint order made under this section in accordance with this section` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order is in force` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person acts in contravention of or fails to comply with the order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.8(9) the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    IF `the person is served with a restraint order made under this section in accordance with this section` AND `the order is in force` AND `the person acts in contravention of or fails to comply with the order`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the offence is that of a person "on whom a restraint order made under this section is served in accordance with this section and who, while the order is in force, acts in contravention of or fails to comply with the order"

@ref Criminal Code s 490.8(9) (src:10811-10814)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 490.8(9) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

@ref Criminal Code s 490.8(9) (src:10811-10814)
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 490.8(9)(a) the punishment on conviction on indictment` MEANS Punishment WITH
    `mode` IS `by indictment`
    `maximum imprisonment` IS `imprisonment for a term of` `five years`
    `minimum imprisonment` IS `no imprisonment is stated`
    `maximum fine` IS `no fine is stated`
    `minimum fine` IS `no fine is stated`

@ref Criminal Code s 490.8(9) (src:10811-10814)
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 490.8(9)(b) the punishment on summary conviction` MEANS Punishment WITH
    `mode` IS `on summary conviction`
    `maximum imprisonment` IS `no imprisonment is stated`   -- paragraph (b) states no penalty: the general penalty is in another part (section 787), not among the sources
    `minimum imprisonment` IS `no imprisonment is stated`
    `maximum fine` IS `no fine is stated`
    `minimum fine` IS `no fine is stated`

§ `490.81 Management order`

-- src:10815 | Management order
-- src:10816 | 490.81 (1) With respect to offence-related property other than a controlled substance within the meaning of the Controlled Drugs and Substances Act or cannabis as defined in subsection 2(1) of the Cannabis Act, on application of the Attorney General or of any other person with the written consent of the Attorney General, a judge or justice in the case of offence-related property seized under section 487, or a judge in the case of offence-related property restrained under section 490.8, may, if he or she is of the opinion that the circumstances so require,
-- src:10817 | (a) appoint a person to take control of and to manage or otherwise deal with all or part of the property in accordance with the directions of the judge or justice; and
-- src:10818 | (b) require any person having possession of that property to give possession of the property to the person appointed under paragraph (a).
@ref Criminal Code s 490.81(1) (src:10815-10818)
DECLARE `s 490.81(1) applicant` IS ONE OF
    `s 490.81(1) the Attorney General`
    `s 490.81(1) another person with the written consent of the Attorney General`
    `s 490.81(1) another person without that consent`

@ref Criminal Code s 490.81(1) (src:10815-10818)
DECLARE `s 490.81(1) how the property is held` IS ONE OF
    `s 490.81(1) offence-related property seized under section 487`
    `s 490.81(1) offence-related property restrained under section 490.8`
    `s 490.81(1) other property`

@ref Criminal Code s 490.81(1) (src:10815-10818)
DECLARE `s 490.81(1) who makes the order` IS ONE OF
    `s 490.81(1) a judge`
    `s 490.81(1) a justice`
    `s 490.81(1) another person`

@ref Criminal Code s 490.81(1) (src:10815-10818)
GIVEN `the property is a controlled substance within the meaning of the Controlled Drugs and Substances Act or cannabis as defined in subsection 2(1) of the Cannabis Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      applicant IS A `s 490.81(1) applicant`
      held IS A `s 490.81(1) how the property is held`
      maker IS A `s 490.81(1) who makes the order`
      `he or she is of the opinion that the circumstances so require` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.81(1) the judge or justice may appoint a person to manage the property and require its possessor to give possession` MEANS
    IF `the property is a controlled substance within the meaning of the Controlled Drugs and Substances Act or cannabis as defined in subsection 2(1) of the Cannabis Act`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "With respect to offence-related property other than a controlled substance within the meaning of the Controlled Drugs and Substances Act or cannabis as defined in subsection 2(1) of the Cannabis Act" (fork F11: "other than" read as an exclusion)
    ELSE IF applicant EQUALS `s 490.81(1) another person without that consent`
            OR (NOT ((held EQUALS `s 490.81(1) offence-related property seized under section 487` AND (maker EQUALS `s 490.81(1) a judge` OR maker EQUALS `s 490.81(1) a justice`))
                     OR (held EQUALS `s 490.81(1) offence-related property restrained under section 490.8` AND maker EQUALS `s 490.81(1) a judge`)))
            OR (NOT `he or she is of the opinion that the circumstances so require`)
         THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on application of the Attorney General or of any other person with the written consent of the Attorney General, a judge or justice in the case of offence-related property seized under section 487, or a judge in the case of offence-related property restrained under section 490.8, may, if he or she is of the opinion that the circumstances so require" (fork F5)
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:10819 | Appointment of Minister of Public Works and Government Services
-- src:10820 | (2) When the Attorney General of Canada so requests, a judge or justice appointing a person under subsection (1) shall appoint the Minister of Public Works and Government Services.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.81(2) (src:10819-10820)
DECLARE `s 490.81(2) action` IS ONE OF `s 490.81(2) appoint the Minister of Public Works and Government Services`

@ref Criminal Code s 490.81(2) (src:10819-10820)
GIVEN `the Attorney General of Canada so requests` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.81(2) the judge or justice shall appoint the Minister of Public Works and Government Services` MEANS
    IF `the Attorney General of Canada so requests` THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "When the Attorney General of Canada so requests" [marginal (a)]

@ref Criminal Code s 490.81(2) (src:10819-10820)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `s 490.81(2) action`
`s 490.81(2) the duty of a judge` MEANS
    PARTY `a judge`
    MUST `s 490.81(2) appoint the Minister of Public Works and Government Services`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `a judge` BECAUSE "the Attorney General of Canada requested it and the judge or justice did not appoint the Minister of Public Works and Government Services"

-- src:10821 | Power to manage
-- src:10822 | (3) The power to manage or otherwise deal with property under subsection (1) includes
-- src:10823 | (a) the power to make an interlocutory sale of perishable or rapidly depreciating property;
-- src:10824 | (b) the power to destroy, in accordance with subsections (4) to (7), property that has little or no value; and
-- src:10825 | (c) the power to have property, other than real property or a conveyance, forfeited to Her Majesty in accordance with subsection (7.1).
@ref Criminal Code s 490.81(3) (src:10821-10825)
DECLARE `s 490.81(3) power` IS ONE OF
    `s 490.81(3)(a) the power to make an interlocutory sale of perishable or rapidly depreciating property`
    `s 490.81(3)(b) the power to destroy, in accordance with subsections (4) to (7), property that has little or no value`
    `s 490.81(3)(c) the power to have property, other than real property or a conveyance, forfeited to Her Majesty in accordance with subsection (7.1)`
    `s 490.81(3) another power`

@ref Criminal Code s 490.81(3) (src:10821-10825)
GIVEN power IS A `s 490.81(3) power`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.81(3) the power to manage or otherwise deal with property includes the power` MEANS
    CONSIDER power
    WHEN `s 490.81(3)(a) the power to make an interlocutory sale of perishable or rapidly depreciating property` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 490.81(3)(b) the power to destroy, in accordance with subsections (4) to (7), property that has little or no value` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 490.81(3)(c) the power to have property, other than real property or a conveyance, forfeited to Her Majesty in accordance with subsection (7.1)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 490.81(3) another power` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "The power to manage or otherwise deal with property under subsection (1) includes"

-- src:10826 | Application for destruction order
-- src:10827 | (4) Before a person who is appointed to manage property destroys property that has little or no value, they shall apply to a court for a destruction order.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.81(4) (src:10826-10827)
DECLARE `s 490.81(4) party` IS ONE OF `s 490.81(4) a person appointed to manage property`   -- not in the core's Party: NEEDS-CORE.md
DECLARE `s 490.81(4) action` IS ONE OF `s 490.81(4) apply to a court for a destruction order`

@ref Criminal Code s 490.81(4) (src:10826-10827)
GIVEN `the person appointed to manage property destroys property that has little or no value` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.81(4) the person appointed to manage property shall apply to a court for a destruction order` MEANS
    IF `the person appointed to manage property destroys property that has little or no value` THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is laid only where "Before a person who is appointed to manage property destroys property that has little or no value, they shall apply to a court for a destruction order"

@ref Criminal Code s 490.81(4) (src:10826-10827)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 490.81(4) party` `s 490.81(4) action`
`s 490.81(4) the duty of a person appointed to manage property` MEANS
    PARTY `s 490.81(4) a person appointed to manage property`
    MUST `s 490.81(4) apply to a court for a destruction order`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 490.81(4) a person appointed to manage property` BECAUSE "the person appointed to manage property destroyed it without applying for a destruction order"

-- src:10828 | Notice
-- src:10829 | (5) Before making a destruction order, a court shall require notice in accordance with subsection (6) to be given to and may hear any person who, in the court’s opinion, appears to have a valid interest in the property.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.81(5) (src:10828-10829)
DECLARE `s 490.81(5) action` IS ONE OF `s 490.81(5) require notice in accordance with subsection (6) to be given to the person`

@ref Criminal Code s 490.81(5) (src:10828-10829)
GIVEN `before making a destruction order, the court is of the opinion that the person appears to have a valid interest in the property` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.81(5) the court shall require notice to be given` MEANS
    IF `before making a destruction order, the court is of the opinion that the person appears to have a valid interest in the property` THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is laid only where "any person who, in the court’s opinion, appears to have a valid interest in the property"

@ref Criminal Code s 490.81(5) (src:10828-10829)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `s 490.81(5) action`
`s 490.81(5) the duty of the court` MEANS
    PARTY `the court`
    MUST `s 490.81(5) require notice in accordance with subsection (6) to be given to the person`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the court` BECAUSE "the court did not require notice to be given to the person with a valid interest"

-- src:10830 | Manner of giving notice
-- src:10831 | (6) A notice shall
-- src:10832 | (a) be given in the manner that the court directs or that may be specified in the rules of the court; and
-- src:10833 | (b) specify the effective period of the notice that the court considers reasonable or that may be set out in the rules of the court.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.81(6) (src:10830-10833)
GIVEN `(a) the notice is given in the manner that the court directs or that may be specified in the rules of the court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `(b) the notice specifies the effective period of the notice that the court considers reasonable or that may be set out in the rules of the court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.81(6) the notice is as the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `(a) the notice is given in the manner that the court directs or that may be specified in the rules of the court` AND `(b) the notice specifies the effective period of the notice that the court considers reasonable or that may be set out in the rules of the court`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A notice shall (a) be given in the manner that the court directs"

-- src:10834 | Destruction order
-- src:10835 | (7) A court shall order that the property be destroyed if it is satisfied that the property has little or no financial or other value.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.81(7) (src:10834-10835)
DECLARE `s 490.81(7) action` IS ONE OF `s 490.81(7) order that the property be destroyed`

@ref Criminal Code s 490.81(7) (src:10834-10835)
GIVEN `the court is satisfied that the property has little or no financial or other value` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.81(7) the court shall order that the property be destroyed` MEANS
    IF `the court is satisfied that the property has little or no financial or other value`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A court shall order that the property be destroyed if it is satisfied that the property has little or no financial or other value" [marginal (a)]

@ref Criminal Code s 490.81(7) (src:10834-10835)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 490.81(7) action`
`s 490.81(7) the duty of the court` MEANS
    PARTY `the court`
    MUST `s 490.81(7) order that the property be destroyed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the court` BECAUSE "the court was satisfied that the property has little or no value and did not order it destroyed"

-- src:10836 | Forfeiture order
-- src:10837 | (7.1) On application by a person who is appointed to manage the property, a court shall order that the property, other than real property or a conveyance, be forfeited to Her Majesty to be disposed of or otherwise dealt with in accordance with the law if
-- src:10838 | (a) a notice is given or published in the manner that the court directs or that may be specified in the rules of the court;
-- src:10839 | (b) the notice specifies a period of 60 days during which a person may make an application to the court asserting their interest in the property; and
-- src:10840 | (c) during that period, no one makes such an application.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.81(7.1) (src:10836-10840)
DECLARE `s 490.81(7.1) action` IS ONE OF `s 490.81(7.1) order that the property be forfeited to Her Majesty to be disposed of or otherwise dealt with in accordance with the law`

@ref Criminal Code s 490.81(7.1) (src:10836-10840)
GIVEN `the application is made by a person who is appointed to manage the property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the property is not real property or a conveyance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `(a) a notice is given or published in the manner that the court directs or that may be specified in the rules of the court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `(b) the notice specifies a period of 60 days during which a person may make an application to the court asserting their interest in the property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `(c) during that period, no one makes such an application` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.81(7.1) the court shall order the property forfeited to Her Majesty` MEANS
    IF `the application is made by a person who is appointed to manage the property` AND `the property is not real property or a conveyance` AND `(a) a notice is given or published in the manner that the court directs or that may be specified in the rules of the court` AND `(b) the notice specifies a period of 60 days during which a person may make an application to the court asserting their interest in the property` AND `(c) during that period, no one makes such an application`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a court shall order that the property, other than real property or a conveyance, be forfeited to Her Majesty to be disposed of or otherwise dealt with in accordance with the law if" [marginal (a)]

@ref Criminal Code s 490.81(7.1) (src:10836-10840)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 490.81(7.1) action`
`s 490.81(7.1) the duty of the court to order the forfeiture` MEANS
    PARTY `the court`
    MUST `s 490.81(7.1) order that the property be forfeited to Her Majesty to be disposed of or otherwise dealt with in accordance with the law`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the court` BECAUSE "the conditions were met and the court did not order the property forfeited"

-- src:10841 | When management order ceases to have effect
-- src:10842 | (8) A management order ceases to have effect when the property that is the subject of the management order is returned in accordance with the law, destroyed or forfeited to Her Majesty.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.81(8) (src:10841-10842)
GIVEN `the property that is the subject of the management order is returned in accordance with the law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the property that is the subject of the management order is destroyed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the property that is the subject of the management order is forfeited to Her Majesty` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.81(8) the management order ceases to have effect` MEANS
    IF `the property that is the subject of the management order is returned in accordance with the law` OR `the property that is the subject of the management order is destroyed` OR `the property that is the subject of the management order is forfeited to Her Majesty`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A management order ceases to have effect when the property that is the subject of the management order is returned in accordance with the law, destroyed or forfeited to Her Majesty" [marginal (a)]

-- src:10843 | For greater certainty
-- src:10844 | (8.1) For greater certainty, if property that is the subject of a management order is sold, the management order applies to the net proceeds of the sale.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.81(8.1) (src:10843-10844)
GIVEN `the property that is the subject of a management order is sold` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.81(8.1) the management order applies to the net proceeds of the sale` MEANS
    IF `the property that is the subject of a management order is sold`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if property that is the subject of a management order is sold, the management order applies to the net proceeds of the sale"

-- src:10845 | Application to vary conditions
-- src:10846 | (9) The Attorney General may at any time apply to the judge or justice to cancel or vary any condition to which a management order is subject, but may not apply to vary an appointment made under subsection (2).
@ref Criminal Code s 490.81(9) (src:10845-10846)
GIVEN `the application is to cancel or vary a condition to which the management order is subject` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is to vary an appointment made under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.81(9) the Attorney General may apply to the judge or justice` MEANS
    IF `the application is to vary an appointment made under subsection (2)`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but may not apply to vary an appointment made under subsection (2)"
    ELSE IF `the application is to cancel or vary a condition to which the management order is subject`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may at any time apply to the judge or justice to cancel or vary any condition to which a management order is subject"

§ `490.9 Sections 489.1 and 490 applicable; recognizance`

-- src:10847 | Sections 489.1 and 490 applicable
-- src:10848 | 490.9 (1) Subject to sections 490.1 to 490.7, sections 489.1 and 490 apply, with any modifications that the circumstances require, to any offence-related property that is the subject of a restraint order made under section 490.8.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.9(1) (src:10847-10848)
GIVEN `the property is offence-related property that is the subject of a restraint order made under section 490.8` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.9(1) sections 489.1 and 490 apply to the property` MEANS
    IF `the property is offence-related property that is the subject of a restraint order made under section 490.8`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "sections 489.1 and 490 apply, with any modifications that the circumstances require, to any offence-related property that is the subject of a restraint order made under section 490.8"

-- src:10849 | Recognizance
-- src:10850 | (2) Where, pursuant to subsection (1), an order is made under paragraph 490(9)(c) for the return of any offence-related property that is the subject of a restraint order under section 490.8, the judge or justice making the order may require the applicant for the order to enter into a recognizance before the judge or justice, with or without sureties, in any amount and with any conditions that the judge or justice directs and, where the judge or justice considers it appropriate, require the applicant to deposit with the judge or justice any sum of money or other valuable security that the judge or justice directs.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.9(2) (src:10849-10850)
GIVEN `an order is made under paragraph 490(9)(c) for the return of the offence-related property that is the subject of a restraint order under section 490.8` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.9(2) (recognizance) the judge or justice may require the applicant to enter into a recognizance` MEANS
    IF `an order is made under paragraph 490(9)(c) for the return of the offence-related property that is the subject of a restraint order under section 490.8`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where, pursuant to subsection (1), an order is made under paragraph 490(9)(c) for the return of any offence-related property" [may-where]

-- src:10849 | Recognizance
-- src:10850 | (2) Where, pursuant to subsection (1), an order is made under paragraph 490(9)(c) for the return of any offence-related property that is the subject of a restraint order under section 490.8, the judge or justice making the order may require the applicant for the order to enter into a recognizance before the judge or justice, with or without sureties, in any amount and with any conditions that the judge or justice directs and, where the judge or justice considers it appropriate, require the applicant to deposit with the judge or justice any sum of money or other valuable security that the judge or justice directs.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.9(2) (src:10849-10850)
GIVEN `an order is made under paragraph 490(9)(c) for the return of the offence-related property that is the subject of a restraint order under section 490.8` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge or justice considers it appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.9(2) (deposit) the judge or justice may require the applicant to deposit a sum of money or other valuable security` MEANS
    IF `an order is made under paragraph 490(9)(c) for the return of the offence-related property that is the subject of a restraint order under section 490.8` AND `the judge or justice considers it appropriate`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the judge or justice considers it appropriate, require the applicant to deposit with the judge or justice any sum of money or other valuable security" [may-where]
